          "variant": null,
          "code": "reusable_sample_value",
          "description_paragraphs": [
            "A new sample handle corresponds to an independent draw of the hidden sample $Z$. Given its handle and $x\\in \\mathbb{R}^d$, the interface returns the exact sample value $F(x;Z)$. The algorithm observes only handles and numerical values, not the underlying sample data or the complete sample function.",
            "Sample handles may be retained for arbitrarily many paid evaluations. Responses using the same handle come from the same function, and distinct handles are independent.",
            "The full function $\\psi$ is known. Composite mirror-descent subproblems over the intersection of a local ball with $\\operatorname{dom}\\psi$, and the final minimization of an affine function plus $\\psi$, are free. These specific convex optimization operations are included among the auxiliary permissions.",
            "The public inputs are $d$, $L$, $\\Delta$, $\\rho$, $\\gamma$, $\\varepsilon$, $\\psi$, $x_0$, together with the sets, kernels and auxiliary operations explicitly declared above. Information about the unknown objective and any undisclosed sample distribution is obtained only through the stated interface."
          ]
        },
        "output": {
